prompt:
Kreative Studio pose editor, image check part (STU-PE3). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions, never at the top level (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Do not change the test file. Return the whole file.

Write public/js/pose/posecheck.js (NAME = posecheck): compare the keypoints a detector (DWPose) found in a generated image with the target pose's keypoints, bone by bone, as 2D angles on screen. No need() calls are needed in this file.

Keypoints object (kp): {width, height, body: 18 points, left: 21 points, right: 21 points}; a point is [x, y] in pixels or null. Body order is OpenPose BODY18: 0 nose, 1 neck, 2 r_shoulder, 3 r_elbow, 4 r_wrist, 5 l_shoulder, 6 l_elbow, 7 l_wrist, 8 r_hip, 9 r_knee, 10 r_ankle, 11 l_hip, 12 l_knee, 13 l_ankle, 14 r_eye, 15 l_eye, 16 r_ear, 17 l_ear.

Export:
- BONES: exactly this list (a and b are lists of body indices; a point made from several indices is their average):
  [{name: 'torso', a: [1], b: [8, 11], joint: 'spine'}, {name: 'head', a: [1], b: [0], joint: 'neck'},
   {name: 'l_upper_arm', a: [5], b: [6], joint: 'l_shoulder'}, {name: 'l_forearm', a: [6], b: [7], joint: 'l_elbow'},
   {name: 'r_upper_arm', a: [2], b: [3], joint: 'r_shoulder'}, {name: 'r_forearm', a: [3], b: [4], joint: 'r_elbow'},
   {name: 'l_thigh', a: [11], b: [12], joint: 'l_hip'}, {name: 'l_shin', a: [12], b: [13], joint: 'l_knee'},
   {name: 'r_thigh', a: [8], b: [9], joint: 'r_hip'}, {name: 'r_shin', a: [9], b: [10], joint: 'r_knee'}]
- fromOpenPose(json, opts = {}): json is OpenPose JSON {canvas_width, canvas_height, people: [{pose_keypoints_2d, hand_left_keypoints_2d, hand_right_keypoints_2d}]} or a list of such objects (ComfyUI POSE_KEYPOINT; take the first). If there is no object or people is empty, throw new Error('No person in the keypoints.'). person = people[0]. minConf = opts.minConf ?? 0.3. read(arr, n): n points; point i is [arr[3i], arr[3i+1]] with confidence arr[3i+2]; it is null when arr is missing or too short, when the confidence < minConf, or when x === 0 and y === 0. Return {width: canvas_width, height: canvas_height, body: read(pose_keypoints_2d, 18), left: read(hand_left_keypoints_2d, 21), right: read(hand_right_keypoints_2d, 21)}.
- swapSides(kp): a new kp (input unchanged) with body pairs [2,5], [3,6], [4,7], [8,11], [9,12], [10,13], [14,15], [16,17] swapped and left/right hands swapped; 0 and 1 stay.
- compare(target, detected, opts = {}): tol = opts.tol ?? 20. one(det) builds bones: for each BONES entry b: ta/tb = the target's a and b points, da/db = the detected ones (null if any index is null). If ta or tb is null: {name, joint, err: null, status: 'skip'}. Else if da or db is null: {..., err: null, status: 'missing'}. Else err = the angle in degrees (0..180) between vectors tb - ta and db - da (use Math.atan2 of the cross and dot products), rounded to 0.1 (Math.round(x * 10) / 10); status = err > tol ? 'wrong' : 'ok'. Keys in this order: name, joint, err, status.
  bones = one(detected). If opts.swap !== false: alt = one(swapSides(detected)); use alt (swapped = true) when it has fewer 'wrong' bones, or the same number and a smaller sum of err over the bones with a number. Otherwise swapped = false.
  pass = no bone is 'wrong', and when opts.strict also none is 'missing'. worst = the name of the 'wrong' bone with the largest err, or null.
  Return {pass, swapped, worst, tol, bones}.
